@startuml adxl345-startup
' Bringing the accelerometer up, and why the order of the four writes is
' not a matter of taste. Grounded in Src/adxl345.c (adxl345_begin) and in
' the ADXL345 datasheet Rev 0, Table 16 for the registers, Table 6 for the
' rate codes and Table 19 for the FIFO modes.

title Start-up, in the order the part asks for

skinparam shadowing false

start

:read DEVID (0x00);

if (answered 0xE5?) then (no)
  :return WRONG_DEVICE;
  note right
    Nothing is configured.
    Something else lives at this
    address, or the bus reads as
    zero because nothing is there.
  end note
  stop
else (yes)
endif

note right
  Everything below happens while
  the part is STILL IN STANDBY.
  It powers up that way and the
  datasheet asks for the settings
  to be in place before it runs.
end note

:BW_RATE   = 0x0D   (800 Hz, 400 Hz bandwidth);
:DATA_FORMAT = 0x09 (full resolution, plus or minus 4 g);
:FIFO_CTL  = 0x80   (stream mode, 32 deep);

:POWER_CTL = 0x08   (measure);
note right
  LAST. Start it any earlier and the
  first samples are taken at 100 Hz
  with the FIFO bypassed, which are
  the reset settings.
end note

:return OK;

stop

legend bottom
  Stream mode is what removes the need for a timer driver.
  The sensor keeps its own 800 Hz pace and holds the latest
  32 samples, so the firmware never has to arrive on time,
  only often enough.
endlegend

@enduml
